  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -2913,8 +2913,21 @@ upon the conversation index and values inside the request packets.\n     }\n \n \n+2.2.6 Registering with Analyze → Conversation Filter\n \n-2.3 Dynamic conversation dissector registration.\n+If your protocol defines conversations (e.g., using `conversation_new()`), you can register it with the “Analyze → Conversation Filter” menu in Wireshark.\n+\n+To do this, use the `conversation_filter_add()` function declared in `epan/conversation_filter.h`. This allows users to quickly apply a display filter to traffic belonging to that conversation from the GUI.\n+\n+Basic example:\n+\n+```c\n+conversation_t *conversation = find_or_create_conversation(pinfo);\n+conversation_filter_add(conversation, \"myproto\");\n+\n+\n+\n+2.3 Dynamic conversation dissector registratiogn.\n \n \n NOTE:   This sections assumes that all information is available to\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/README.dissector",
